💡 **SUGGESTION: make the lockstep check iterate `stubs` too (or fix the doc's mechanism claim)**

This doc says "the lockstep, factory_ref-echo and secrets checks below iterate this map" — after `59d3e9af` only echo and secrets do; the lockstep test still hardcodes its three locals:

```dart
final a = pinnedRef(teammate, 'factory-teammate.yml');
final b = pinnedRef(sm, 'factory-sm.yml');
final c = pinnedRef(merge, 'factory-merge.yml');
```

The stated guarantee still holds (an unlisted new stub escapes all three checks either way, since a/b/c are fixed), so this is polish, not a gap. But migrating the lockstep test to the map makes the doc true, gives a 4th stub a single edit point, and keeps skew assertions from growing by hand:

```dart
test('all stubs pin the SAME factory ref (lockstep)', () {
  final refs = stubs.values.map((e) => pinnedRef(e.$1, e.$2)).toSet();
  expect(refs, hasLength(1),
      reason: 'teammate/SM/merge factories must not skew apart — '
          'the SM dispatches teammate and the merge fast path runs '
          'mergeBot.js from the same pinned pack');
});
```

(Or, minimally, reword the doc to "the factory_ref-echo and secrets checks below iterate this map".)

